WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.720
Kurakawa Mari died seven years ago.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:04.880
She died?

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.360
When the doctor performed a C-section on Mari's
mother, Mari had already stopped breathing.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:17.250
Mari, if Kurakawa Mari died,
then who might you be?

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.420
I'm Kurakawa Mari...

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.050
What is the meaning of this, Kei?

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:28.460
Mari, you were created
with someone's ability, right?

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:32.360
The flow of time makes a continuous sound

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.090
I'm pretty sure your mother gained
the ability when her real daughter died.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:37.850
The ability to create a clone of her dead daughter.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.490
It's a melody that invites the coming future
The ability to create a clone of her dead daughter.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:41.600
You're the clone, right?
It's a melody that invites the coming future

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.350
It's a melody that invites the coming future

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:50.040
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.650
Tsushima...
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:52.330
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:53.970
I work for the Bureau.
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.910
I came to pick up Kurakawa Mari.
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:56.160
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:56.740
Now, let's go.
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:57.510
I tried asking myself for an answer
Now, let's go.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:58.830
I tried asking myself for an answer

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.840
Go where?
I tried asking myself for an answer

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.220
Where she needs to be.
I tried asking myself for an answer

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:03.330
Will Mari's mother be there?
I tried asking myself for an answer

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.680
Will Mari's mother be there?

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.540
She won't be coming back anymore.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.210
Here, in the middle of ideals and reality
She won't be coming back anymore.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:08.680
Here, in the middle of ideals and reality

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.840
She left Mari in the Bureau's care and left this town.
Here, in the middle of ideals and reality

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.940
Was it to forget Mari's existence?
Here, in the middle of ideals and reality

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:15.630
Yes.
Here, in the middle of ideals and reality

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:15.930
Yes.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:16.930
I see. That's terrible to hear.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.790
The hands of the clock are being constantly moved
I see. That's terrible to hear.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.480
What is that supposed to mean?
The hands of the clock are being constantly moved

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.180
The hands of the clock are being constantly moved

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:27.580
Somewhere along the line, Mari's mother stopped
being able to believe that Mari was her own child.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.350
I'll do anything to erase all sadness

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.270
"Somewhere along the line," meaning what?
I'll do anything to erase all sadness

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:34.860
Mari's father could never accept
Mari as his own daughter.
I'll do anything to erase all sadness

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:35.080
Mari's father could never accept
Mari as his own daughter.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.160
He took off after putting up with it for three years.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.360
Even if it means going back down the passage of dark stairs

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.490
It was around that time.
Even if it means going back down the passage of dark stairs

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:40.220
Even if it means going back down the passage of dark stairs

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:44.080
It was the Bureau that suggested
she should leave Sakurada, right?

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:44.570
Even if it means going back down the passage of dark stairs

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.330
The ability to create lives is something
that must be kept under wraps.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:49.510
There's something I want to protect no matter what

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:53.420
If she leaves Sakurada, then her memories
about her ability will disappear.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:54.330
What are you planning to do with Mari?
There's something I want to protect no matter what

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:55.320
What are you planning to do with Mari?

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:55.840
She'll grow up as a normal child.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.550
I'll say that out loud
She'll grow up as a normal child.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.010
I'll say that out loud

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.390
The Bureau decided it was best
to keep a problematic ability secret.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.140
Believing that fate will bring us together again

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:08.320
To achieve that, they took away the mother's memories
of Mari, and turned a little girl into a victim.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.440
That means you chose to look at the bigger picture.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.540
That's the Bureau.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.570
Do you really think that's right?

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:18.700
There's nothing right about a child crying.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.940
Was it something you had
to choose despite it being wrong?

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:23.690
It's not like that.

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:26.910
It isn't something we should have chosen,
and that's why it's wrong.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:30.570
You're contradicting yourself.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.420
What do <i>you</i> want to do?

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.100
I don't want to do anything.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.380
I don't even want to get involved in this mess.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.050
But you <i>are</i> involved.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:42.420
My job means doing things I don't want to do.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.930
We're done here.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.230
I'm taking Mari with me.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.940
You're not the one who gets to choose that.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.890
You choose, Haruki.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.690
Are you going to hand Mari over to the Bureau?

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:04.660
Asai Kei, please let go of him.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.930
And you're okay with that?

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:06.660
Yes.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:13.420
Based on the circumstances, I've determined
that Mari has to be taken care of by the Bureau.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.710
But Haruki isn't able to help anyone.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.050
Haruki Misora, can you really be that indifferent?

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.880
Of course not.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.000
Then choose.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.940
Choose with your own feelings.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.290
Not on a passing whim, but as a necessity.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.800
Have your own, clear will.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.220
You have to choose a side.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.710
I want to help Mari, but...

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.160
If that's what you want, then let's help her.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.940
Is it possible?

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.660
With our abilities, yeah.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.460
With the memories we gained today,
we'll aim for a happier ending.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.880
We can redo this.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.630
Haruki, it's time to reset.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:01.690
Reset.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:12.270
Haruki, you need to remember your feelings.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.270
Is that so?

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.820
Yeah, so let's begin.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:17.520
Okay.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.930
I'm starting now.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:24.930
Let's go.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:41.490
I remembered all of the sadness
I was supposed to feel soon.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.760
Let's go erase the girl's tears.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.570
We'll rid this world of such things.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:55.020
That's the plan that I came up with.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.980
Would you help us out, too, Sakagami?

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.610
Uh, no... I can't.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.090
It will be in defiance of the Bureau, wouldn't it?

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:05.050
It'll be okay if you get permission, right?

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:10.080
As things stand, Mari's mother will be leaving
Sakurada on Saturday, which is in two days.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:13.530
We need to solve everything before then.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:17.580
But still... I can't defy the Bureau, sorry.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.800
Do we need him no matter what?

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.340
Yeah. I want his ability at all costs.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:30.310
Sakagami Yousuke won't use his ability for us
unless he has the Bureau's permission, right?

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.170
That's his rule.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:35.060
You use the word "rule" often.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.440
Would you tell me what your rules are?

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.700
Among my rules are three big ones.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:45.650
I basically decide on things
according to these three rules.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.220
What's the first rule?

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:53.600
If something has a probability of causing a strongly
negative effect on my surroundings, I refuse.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.890
Which means you won't cause trouble for anyone.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:57.670
How about the second?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:03.420
I'll agree to a proposition so long
as it doesn't violate the first rule.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.500
In other words, you'll follow someone's instructions.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:07.430
And the third rule?

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:11.930
When I come across someone crying,
I use my reset ability.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:18.190
Haruki, do you know the Three Laws of Robotics?

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:19.480
No.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:23.480
The First Law states that a robot
may not harm a human being.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:27.150
The Second Law states that a robot must
obey orders given to it by a human being.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.770
And the Third Law states that a robot
must protect its own existence.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:34.190
The first and second laws are exactly like your rules.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:36.410
But the third one is different.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.890
That's what's wonderful.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.420
What does that mean?

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.670
It means you're a human being.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.170
I don't really follow.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:47.960
Well, it's fine if you don't.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.580
There's a Zeroth Law in the three laws for androids.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.760
There wasn't one at first, but it was
added later when it was deemed necessary.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.190
Can you guess what it is?

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.210
No, I have no idea.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:02.970
Try thinking about it.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:07.820
If you were to make a Zeroth rule for yourself,
what kind of rule would it be?

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.780
What do you want to do with Haruki Misora?

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.200
What do you mean?

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.430
You've become interested in Haruki Misora.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:21.170
You thought her personality was the ideal good.

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:25.070
She doesn't care about protecting herself,
her image, or her ego,

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.130
and she doesn't even want to be loved by others.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:30.460
She's pure like purity itself.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:34.010
She's so purely good that she
doesn't even realize it herself.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:36.510
She's the most beautiful being.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:41.160
And yet, you're trying to give her feelings.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.220
That's right.

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:43.980
You're contradicting yourself.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:49.490
You yourself are trying to destroy the very
thing you believe is the most beautiful.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.260
You may be right.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:52.110
So why?

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:55.490
I don't know why. It's just a whim.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:58.170
You're a liar.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.010
You won't believe me?

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:04.420
I believe you from the bottom of my heart.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:10.170
You wish for Haruki to become a normal
girl who can laugh and cry, don't you?

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:15.060
Even as far as putting her own
happiness above being your ideal.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.810
It's just more convenient that way.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:21.310
For getting my hands on her reset ability, I mean.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.770
You really are such a liar.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:29.400
Are you okay? Are you feeling sick?

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:31.390
I wonder...

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:35.740
I might not be okay.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.040
Haruki, it's time to save.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:45.750
Save.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.550
Will everything really be all right?

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.720
That guy is kind.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:56.010
And a kind adult will listen
to a child's selfish demands.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.890
I received a message in my mind.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:05.480
It told me to come here.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:07.860
That's his ability.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:11.320
He can make his voice reach whoever
he wants, whenever he wants.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.530
What a self-serving ability.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.360
There's something I'd like to ask of you.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.660
We want to help Kurakawa Mari.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.370
Would you give us permission to do so?

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:20.740
I can't.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.830
The decision was already made.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:26.500
Sakurada's abilities can't be manifested
unless you truly desire to use them.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:31.500
There's no way a mother's
love for her child is wrong.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:37.680
Are you trying to threaten me?

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:38.470
Quite the opposite.

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:42.390
What are you doing?!

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.600
Please give us permission to use
an ability on Mari's mother.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.310
I don't have that kind of authority.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.110
It's okay even if you lie.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:56.400
I won't stop until you give us permission.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.030
What are you thinking?!

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.450
You'll die!

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.320
That's true.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.790
I implore you. It's okay if it's just lip service.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.080
Please say that you'll give us permission.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.290
All right.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.090
Please say it again, so that it's crystal clear.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.550
All right, I'll give you permission.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:19.680
It's okay for us to use Sakagami's
ability on Mari's mother, correct?

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.720
Yeah, I don't mind.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.390
Thank you very much.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.930
You're crazy.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:30.100
No matter what I say,
the Bureau won't give permission!

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.020
I know that.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.780
Haruki, would you please reset?

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:37.780
Reset.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:45.370
Let's get out of here. She reset just now.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.540
Wait, seriously?

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.790
Tomoki, cancel that message to Tsushima.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:51.920
A prank call?! You're terrible.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.250
What did you do?

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.590
Before the reset,

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:58.260
Tomoki sent a message to Sakagami
saying he had permission to use his ability.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:02.510
We've already tested earlier if Tomoki's
ability would work even after a reset.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.440
Mari's mother just left the hospital at 10:36 a.m.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:19.150
She's in a black car. We're moving out now.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.280
Good luck.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.410
That's a handy ability.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:23.950
And there's no calling fee.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.660
It's a one-way call, though.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.500
Haruki!

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.250
Are you sick?

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:38.260
No, I came to see you.

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.480
Hello.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.230
Pardon me, but who are you?

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:54.690
I'm Mari's friend.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.690
Do you need something?

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.320
I'm here to stop you.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:08.990
Are you really fine with forgetting all about Mari?

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.500
She'd be better off without me.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.500
A mother who can't even love her own child...

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.210
All I can give her is unhappiness.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:17.590
Mari loves you.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:19.800
But I hurt Mari.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:23.340
You not being around hurts her even more.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:28.640
There's a way for everyone to be happy.
Will you work with us?

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:30.930
What does that mean?

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.640
All you need to do is love her back.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.560
I can't do that.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.810
Why not?

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:40.440
Are you that repulsed by what
you've created with your ability?

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.070
How do you know about that?

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:45.110
Haruki Misora is Mari's friend.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:49.410
She also learned about her true identity,
yet she still remains her friend.

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.830
You wouldn't understand.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.960
The real Mari died.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:56.880
My child wasn't even allowed to be born.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:01.880
There's no way I can forget about her
and smile with the Mari I created.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:05.050
Please imagine yourself in her shoes.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:10.640
Suppose you were the one who died,
and the real Mari created an exact clone of you.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:14.850
Would you be sad if Mari loved your clone?

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:16.270
That's not what this is about!

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:18.020
But it is.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:21.110
Mari will be sad, and she won't
have anyone to be happy with.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.950
I'm sure your mother will come back.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.780
She won't.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.700
What makes you think that?

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.120
Because she hates me.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:36.000
She'll love you soon enough—

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.170
no, she'll remember how much she loved you.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:44.300
Mari, wishes are something
you need to say out loud.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.930
Put all your heart into it,
so that everyone can hear you.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:50.180
Go on. Say what you wish to happen.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:55.810
We'll now help you remember the time
when you gave birth to Mari seven years ago.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:14:01.230
Please decide if you really should leave
Sakurada after you remember everything.

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.880
What's going on?

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:32.720
She's under the influence of the most
selfish and beautiful ability I know of.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.720
It's time.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.480
Go on. Say what you wish to happen.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.480
I love my mom!

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.860
I want to stay with her forever!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.330
I'm sorry...

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.290
I'm so sorry!

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.310
Would you happen to be free?

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.770
I'm going to the mountains after this.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:24.820
In this rain?

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.530
So, who do you think is the android?

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:30.400
There isn't an android.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:33.280
No matter how much I racked my brain
over it, everyone was human.

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:38.620
Even so, you're supposed to assume
that there's an android among us!

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:41.540
In that case, everyone's an android.

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:45.670
Every single person is influenced and
molded by somebody else, after all.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:48.420
There's no such thing as a human
who isn't created by humans.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:52.340
That's true. I'm pretty sure it is.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:59.060
Hey, Kei. Why did you ditch your parents
and decide to stay in town?

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:01.520
I was interested in special abilities.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:02.560
That's all?

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:07.770
I used to be like Haruki.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.280
I used to think this world was
made of only very sad rules.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.450
But this town was different.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:17.080
All the rules that I was forced to accept
fell apart before my very eyes.

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:22.870
You stayed in Sakurada to erase the sadness
that you were forced to accept.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:24.670
Just like her,

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:29.170
you wanted the power to erase sadness,
so you desired Haruki's reset ability.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.130
It's very convenient.

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:35.260
Kei, I think you should allow people
to help you a bit more.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:36.760
Help?

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:38.560
You'll feel better if you're helped.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:40.810
I'll give you an excuse for that.

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:47.440
The truth is, you're a foolish person who wants
to keep talking honestly about what is right.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:52.740
And yet, your reason can't apply the
"righteous person" definition to yourself.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:55.740
You wanted to help Mari from the start, didn't you?

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.530
But since you cut yourself off
from your own parents,

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:03.960
you felt it wouldn't be right to condemn
a mother trying to cut off her child, right?

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:07.750
That's why you used Haruki as an excuse.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.800
You're weak, cunning, and the truth
is that you want to be a good person,

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.300
but in your eyes you're a villain
you can't forgive because of that.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:17.720
That's why I'll give you an excuse.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.970
Haruki is changing.

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:24.020
She'll be feeling a lot of things from now on.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.850
She'll learn them from you.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:31.190
You need to become a good person
for Haruki Misora's sake.

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:35.780
Make teaching Haruki Misora
the correct feelings your excuse,

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:37.610
and continue being righteous.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:40.370
I'll do what I can.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:44.370
When I'm with you,
we always end up talking about Haruki.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:47.370
Yeah, you're right. I wonder why.

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.670
Isn't it obvious?

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:53.630
It's because you love Haruki Misora.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.380
That makes sense.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.390
Ah, that's a shame.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.680
I thought you would deny it.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:07.230
Do you want to come see the
sunset after it stops raining?

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.190
I've got a novel to finish reading.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:12.480
Really? Well then, goodbye.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:28.870
You cut your hair.

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.670
I followed your suggestion.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.000
It looks good on you, Haruki.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.260
Thank you.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:41.930
I saw Mari the day before yesterday.

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:44.850
Really? What did you talk about?

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:47.020
We didn't talk.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:47.930
Why not?

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:52.980
She was with her mother, so I thought
it'd be okay to not start a conversation.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:54.480
Well, that's good to hear.

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:55.940
It really is.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.940
You weren't sad?

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.320
No, why do you ask?

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:05.450
I thought about the zeroth rule.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.370
Your rule?

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:10.460
Yes. I found the zeroth rule:

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:13.960
I will follow your lead.

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:19.010
I'll trust in all your actions and words.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:23.430
I think if you hadn't been around,
Mari would still be sad.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:24.470
I don't know about that.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.720
Mari smiled.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:30.810
Just like you said, one girl's tears vanished.

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:33.230
I think that was the right decision.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:36.570
What I wanted to erase were your tears.

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:39.860
You ended up erasing both of our tears, then.

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:41.990
I couldn't do it with my rules.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:45.990
I've finally found my feelings.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:51.500
I'm pretty sure I love you.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:20:01.260
I understand that you trust me,
but that isn't love that you're feeling.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.470
Why do you think that?

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:06.050
I've always been thinking about you.

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:08.350
I'd at least know that about you...

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:12.690
You're not used to having feelings,
so you're confusing the two with one another.

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:16.520
I think it'd be wrong to fall
in love with you as you are now.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:18.190
I don't understand.

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:20.030
Yeah, I didn't think you would.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:24.610
Would it be okay for me to try this out?

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:26.070
Yes.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:36.790
Are you happy?

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.050
I don't know.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:43.760
I'm not happy at all.

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:48.050
If we put our abilities together,
we can erase the tears.

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:50.680
We can overcome most obstacles.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:52.850
Doing that much is enough for now.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:56.440
Let's make that our reason for being together.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.440
Do you have a save?

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:01.440
Yes.

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:12.620
<i>It's possible that might have been a happy event.</i>

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:15.420
<i>But it was something I couldn't accept.</i>

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:20.420
<i>I kissed her only to prove that she doesn't love me,</i>

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.210
<i>so I wanted to erase that.</i>

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>If I'm not mistaken,
Souma should've come here at this time...</i>

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:49.160
Today at dawn, Sumire Souma,
a second-year at Nanasaka Middle School,

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:51.240
was found dead in the river.

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:54.620
Sumire did not return home last night.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:56.670
Police received a missing persons report.

00:21:56.670 --> 00:22:00.630
However, local residents discovered her body
drifting around the mouth of the river.

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:03.550
She was transported to the hospital
where she was confirmed dead.

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:05.920
There were no signs of foul play.

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:10.430
It appears she may have lost her footing
as she was hiking up the mountain in the rain.

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:23.570
I was looking for you.

00:22:23.980 --> 00:22:25.530
I have a request.

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:27.400
Please give me orders to reset.

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:30.280
We can't reset.

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:32.780
We already used your ability.

00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:36.040
We weren't able to avoid her death
even though we did a reset?

00:22:36.620 --> 00:22:37.790
That's not it.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:42.790
Are you... crying?

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:45.510
Yeah,

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:48.090
I'm crying right now.

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:52.600
Are you sad?

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:57.020
I'm not the one who's sad.

00:22:57.020 --> 00:22:59.190
You are.

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:03.110
I'm crying because you're sad.

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:07.740
Summer ended that day.

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:17.580
A service club at Ashiharabashi High School?

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:21.250
Yeah. I'll be the club advisor
and you guys will be the members.

00:23:21.250 --> 00:23:23.290
So we're being monitored?

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:27.010
Don't you two want to help others
with your combined abilities?

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:30.090
What are you going to do, Haruki?

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:34.470
I'll follow your lead, Kei.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:47.570
We're always simply standing in a rain of eternal sadness

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:55.080
That is why I need that warmth of yours

00:23:55.660 --> 00:24:00.540
Life is but a dream we never wake up from

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:08.590
We repeat it over and over, praying for salvation

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:14.180
I kept waiting endlessly for your signal

00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:21.390
To make sure you wouldn't disappear all by yourself

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:25.900
Ah, it doesn't matter where I am or what I'm doing

00:24:25.900 --> 00:24:29.610
My heart can't go against your will

00:24:29.610 --> 00:24:35.240
So I'd follow you even to the ends of the world

00:24:35.240 --> 00:24:42.370
I fell in love with you at the dawn of our new world

00:24:42.370 --> 00:24:49.000
But we kept pushing the hand of the clock backwards

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:56.050
And lost not only time, but our smiles as well

00:24:56.050 --> 00:25:00.140
You're the one who brought it back

00:25:00.140 --> 00:25:07.020
And taught me that even lies can be meaningful
